WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.463
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 2: Family Time.

2
00:00:03.543 --> 00:00:12.099
In this unit you will learn the words for the people in
your family — mum, dad, sister, brother, grandma and grandpa.

3
00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:18.152
You will also learn some breakfast and
fruit words, and how to count from 1 to 10.

4
00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:25.829
You will talk about who is in your family, and about
how families help each other and have fun together.

5
00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:32.103
Say the words out loud — this is about
talking with confidence, not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:38.303
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:46.776
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name the
people in a family (mother, father, sister, brother, grandma,

8
00:00:46.856 --> 00:00:47.881
grandpa, baby).

9
00:00:47.961 --> 00:00:55.175
You will also name some breakfast foods and fruits
(pancakes, cereal, milk, mango, banana, grapes).

10
00:00:55.255 --> 00:01:00.111
You will also count from 1 to 10,
and count backwards from 10 to 1.

11
00:01:00.191 --> 00:01:02.837
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:08.390
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
mother, mum, father, dad, sister, brother.

13
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:13.502
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:13.582 --> 00:01:17.478
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:22.423
The reading sequence includes Breakfast at
Grandma's House and Talk about Family Time.

16
00:01:22.503 --> 00:01:23.228
Read actively.

17
00:01:23.308 --> 00:01:27.195
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:27.275 --> 00:01:30.932
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:31.012 --> 00:01:34.645
The first language focus is Introduce a family member.

20
00:01:34.725 --> 00:01:38.013
Show a family photo or drawing and say who it is.

21
00:01:38.093 --> 00:01:41.245
The word 'my' shows they belong to your family.

22
00:01:41.325 --> 00:01:48.739
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:48.819 --> 00:01:52.692
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:52.772 --> 00:01:57.035
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:01:57.115 --> 00:02:00.340
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.775
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:03.855 --> 00:02:05.330
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:12.022
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:12.102 --> 00:02:15.266
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:22.769
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
